      "statusChangeID": "6074bead95eabc781f742d3f",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "Added the information in https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/udon-networking#data-and-specs\n1. Roughly the round-trip time between the executor and the owner; or if the owner did it, the owner and the receiver.\n2. A race condition; you should expect that any writing done when not-owner will be overridden. Non-owners should not modify things they do not own. However, an UdonBehaviour using Manual sync should be able to do this all in one fell swoop. Using Continuous sync _may_ work in the right order but it's not always expected to do so.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-17T00:25:38.711Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The open beta notification post suggests that SetOwner is instantaneous, but documentation suggests a request is sent to the current owner to confirm whether the ownership transfer is to be allowed.\nIf an ownership transfer request is to be approved by the current owner, this implies an extra two network round-trips will be added to the time before the new owner can begin syncing values. This overhead is crucial to account for in our designs.\nPlease document:\n1. What is the ballpark expected latency between invoking SetOwner and having new values be serialized out? Does it depend on whether an OnOwnershipRequest event is defined?\n2. What happens if you set variables in the time between calling SetOwner and when the OnOwnershipRequest is responded to by the current owner? Is there a possibility that they'll be overwritten by received values in that time?\nThese behaviors aren't currently defined in https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/udon-networking#object-ownership and have significant implications in complex networking designs.",
  "error": null,
